1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,980
Fungi play an important role in ecosystems, are a source of food, and make key contributions to the world of medicine.
真菌在生态系统中扮演着重要角色，是食物的来源，并且对医学界做出关键贡献。

2
00:00:10,980 --> 00:00:15,350
So, why do we know so little about them?
那么，为什么我们对它们知之甚少呢？

3
00:00:15,350 --> 00:00:31,660
An estimated two million fungal species – more than 90% of all fungi – have yet to be described by science, according to Rebecca Morelle, science reporter for the BBC.
据BBC科学记者丽贝卡·莫雷尔称，估计有200万种真菌——占所有真菌的90%以上——尚未被科学描述。

4
00:00:31,660 --> 00:00:43,920
In the UK alone, there are thought to be around 25,000 species of fungi – five or six times more than plants.
仅在英国，就有大约25,000种真菌，是植物种类的五六倍。

5
00:00:43,920 --> 00:00:52,880
Scientists are trying to find out more about this largely unexplored world, but it is challenging.
科学家们正试图进一步探索这个很大程度上未经探索的世界，但这颇具挑战性。

6
00:00:52,880 --> 00:01:08,860
Dr Martyn Ainsworth, a senior researcher from Royal Botanic Gardens, Kew, in London, says: 'We can grow a certain number in the lab, but there is a whole host of fungi that we cannot grow in the lab.
伦敦皇家邱园的高级研究员马丁·安斯沃思博士说："我们可以在实验室中培养一定数量的真菌，但还有大量真菌我们无法在实验室中培养。

7
00:01:08,860 --> 00:01:12,690
This has held back a lot of research.'
这阻碍了许多研究。"

8
00:01:12,690 --> 00:01:20,830
The fact that we know so little about the world of fungi leads many of us to misunderstand them.
我们对真菌世界知之甚少这一事实导致许多人误解它们。"

9
00:01:20,830 --> 00:01:37,040
'A lot of people are afraid of poisonous mushrooms', says Dr Jassy Drakulic, a plant pathologist, 'but only a very small proportion of the thousands of species of fungi in the world can cause disease'.
很多人都害怕毒蘑菇，"植物病理学家贾西·德拉库利奇博士说，"但世界上数千种真菌中，只有极少数能引起疾病。"

10
00:01:37,040 --> 00:01:46,520
Most are harmless and often beneficial, called by some 'the hidden helpers of our environment'.
大多数真菌是无害且常常是有益的，被一些人称为"环境中隐藏的帮手"。

11
00:01:46,520 --> 00:01:58,160
Some fungi provide food and shelter for wildlife, help plants absorb water and nutrients and recycle waste and dead matter.
一些真菌为野生动物提供食物和庇护所，帮助植物吸收水分和养分，并循环利用废物和无机物。

12
00:01:58,160 --> 00:02:08,770
Other types of fungi grow on the roots of trees and plants, forming a huge underground network that helps nourish trees.
其他类型的真菌生长在树木和植物的根部，形成一个巨大的地下网络，帮助滋养树木。

13
00:02:08,770 --> 00:02:16,730
'Fungi are really the behind-the-scenes team that are doing all the work', adds Dr Ainsworth.
安斯沃思博士补充说："真菌实际上是幕后做所有工作的团队。"

14
00:02:16,730 --> 00:02:30,810
So, next time you add mushrooms to your dinner, take a painkiller for a headache, or go for a walk through the woods, remember to thank the living things that made it all possible – fungi.
所以，下次你在晚餐中加入蘑菇，服用止痛药缓解头痛，或者去树林里散步时，记得感谢让这一切成为可能的生物——真菌。
